  "title": "Understanding Sovereign Sustainability in Electronics Supply Chains",
  "summary": "Sovereign sustainability for critical infrastructure refers to a country’s ability to design, operate, maintain, and renew essential systems over the long term without losing control to external actors. Critical infrastructure is sovereignly sustainable when a state can keep essential services running during crises such as war, trade disruption, cyber incidents, or climate shocks, using domestic capabilities and trusted partners, without being exposed to coercion or sudden system failure.",
